 "intro": "Cyzicus, on the Sea of Marmara, winter 73-72 BC, in the Third Mithridatic War. King Mithridates besieges the city with a vast army. You are the consul Lucius Licinius Lucullus, with perhaps 30,000 men.",
 "debrief": "In Plutarch’s and Appian’s accounts, Lucullus refused to fight the huge Pontic army and instead seized ground commanding its supply routes. Through the winter, Mithridates’s men starved. When he sent his cavalry and pack animals away, Lucullus caught them crossing the Rhyndacus in snow, and when Mithridates gave up the siege, Lucullus destroyed his retreating army at the flooded rivers Aesepus and Granicus. Lucullus won the war of hunger without a pitched battle. The other choices are what-ifs.",
